 "summary": "Removing all knowledge-base features (16 OncoKB role/tier features, 4 cancer-hotspot features, and 764 per-gene driver features; 784 of 910 columns) collapses Bio MAF cancer-type performance from 0.662 to 0.514 balanced accuracy (5-fold CV, exact winner XGBoost config, n=8,861). The ablated 126-feature model scores below spectra alone (0.538; paired difference -0.024, 95% CI -0.043 to -0.005). The ranking Sig+MAF > spectra therefore does NOT survive without knowledge-base features: the Bio MAF advantage over spectra on cancer typing depends on curated prior knowledge (driver-gene lists, OncoKB roles, hotspots), not on the remaining annotation features. The TCGA 182-channel spectra matrix was unavailable on this machine, so the spectra arm uses the published benchmark value (0.538) rather than a same-CV rerun, and the ablated Sig+MAF (spectra + 126 non-KB features) could not be built directly."
